CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:“MAYBE SOMETHING NEW WILL ARISE FROM THE DISASTER” Some ev
 ents are so improbable that they are called accidents. Accidents demand an
  explanation. Looking back. Finding the oversight\, the logical flaw\, the
  error. Understanding. And learning. In Take Off \, José Padilla reconstr
 ucts the deadliest disaster in civil aviation history. It took place on Ma
 rch 27\, 1977\, on the runway at Los Rodeos Airport (Tenerife). Two Boeing
  747s collided on the runway before takeoff. 587 people died. That is the 
 accident. Now for the explanation. On stage\, Carlota Gaviño\, Almudena P
 uyo\, Kevin de la Rosa\, and Lucía Trentini seek it out\, bringing passen
 gers\, pilots\, air traffic controllers\, announcers\, and narrator\nCateg
 ory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/e
 n/schedule/take-none-should-have-happened
LOCATION:Naves Matadero\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/take-none-should-have-happe
 ned
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
