 ington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T061500
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T193000
DTSTAMP:20261105T195953Z
UID:efb6c83a7e92521d2839737d78cb@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:What would a free and unified Korean Peninsula look like\, and
  what role should U.S. foreign policy play in making it a reality? Join th
 e International Affairs Society for a conversation on the future of the Ko
 rean Peninsula\, the challenges of reunification\, and the role of interna
 tional cooperation in advancing freedom and security. We’ll be joined by
  Hyun-Seung Lee\, North Korean escapee and founder of the North Korean You
 ng Leaders Assembly\, and Col. David Maxwell (Ret.)\, former U.S. Army Spe
 cial Forces Colonel and Vice President of the Center for Asia Pacific Stra
 tegy.\nCategory: Lectures & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.g
 wu.edu/event/rethinking-korea-policy-towards-a-free-and-unified-korea
LOCATION:1957 E Street NW\, 1957 E St NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/rethinking-korea-policy-towards-a-free-
 and-unified-korea
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
