DESCRIPTION:Introduced by Dr. Racquel Gates (Columbia University) Released
  in 1999\, Spike Lee’s SUMMER OF SAM is based on the 1977 killing spree 
 of David Berkowitz\, known as the Son of Sam. It fuses that year’s heatw
 ave\, Bronx\, New York energy\, sex\, and disco with the fear of a serial 
 killer. It’s Lee’s first film not about Black communities. Mike Imperi
 oli (of THE SOPRANOS fame)\, Victor Colicchio\, and Lee wrote SUMMER OF SA
 M. Actor and star Roger Guenveur Smith talks about the making of the film.
  “’Summer of Sam’ was shot almost entirely in the Country Club secti
 on of the Bronx where the first of the murders took place. ‘You could fe
 el it among the people on the street who had actually lived through th\nCa
 tegory: Film + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emo
 ry-cinematheque-presents-summer-of-sam-1999/
