DESCRIPTION:Grammy Award winner and Musical America 2022 Conductor of the 
 Year Teddy Abrams brings together works by Stravinsky\, Tchaikovsky\, Sara
 h Kirkland Snider\, and Kennedy Center Honoree Michael Tilson Thomas. Call
 ed a voice for this historic moment (The Washington Post)\, bass-baritone 
 Will Liverman joins the orchestra for the world premiere of Sniders Urge\,
  an NSO co-commission setting texts by poet Tracy K. Smith. Stravinskys Sy
 mphonies of Wind Instruments distills music to spare\, haunting phrases\, 
