CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Special\,New Orleans\,United States
DESCRIPTION:To celebrate the opening of Confluence: The Tina Freeman Colle
 ction of Photographs \, join NOMA and PhotoNOLA for  a gallery talk\, an 
 intergenerational conversation about the exhibition and career experiences
  in the field of photography\, as well as a book signing. Panelists for th
 e discussion “The Work We Live With: Women in Photograph” include phot
 ographer\, curator\, and collector Tina Freeman\; photographer and filmmak
 er Sienna Pinderhughes\; and photographer and founder of Women Photograph 
 Daniella Zalcman. The conversation will be moderated by Emilia Mickevicius
 \, Norton Family Assistant Curator of Photography at the Center for Creati
 ve Photography at the University of Arizona and contributin\nCategory: Spe
 cial\nOriginal listing: https://noma.org/event/noma-x-photonola-gallery-ta
 lk-panel-discussion-and-book-signing-celebrating-confluence/
LOCATION:New Orleans Museum of Art\, 1 Collins Diboll Cir\, New Orleans\, 
 LA 70124
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://noma.org/event/noma-x-photonola-gallery-talk-panel-discussion-
 and-book-signing-celebrating-confluence/
